fice/word/2020/wordml/sdtdatahash" xmlns:w16sdtfl="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2024/wordml/sdtformatlock" xmlns:w16se="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2015/wordml/symex" xmlns:wpg="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingGroup" xmlns:wpi="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingInk" xmlns:wne="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2006/wordml" xmlns:wps="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingShape" mc:Ignorable="w14 w15 w16se w16cid w16 w16cex w16sdtdh w16sdtfl w16du wp14"><w:body><w:p w14:paraId="536C0AE3" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="008B4BE7" w:rsidRPr="008B4BE7" w:rsidRDefault="008B4BE7" w:rsidP="009F306F"><w:pPr><w:spacing w:line="360" w:lineRule="auto"/><w:jc w:val="center"/><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:bCs/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr></w:pPr><w:r w:rsidRPr="008B4BE7"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:b/><w:bCs/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t>Title:</w:t></w:r><w:r w:rsidRPr="008B4BE7"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:bCs/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t xml:space="preserve"> Becoming a Professional IT Practitioner</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="3F4B899A" w14:textId="0408A6FB" w:rsidR="009F306F" w:rsidRPr="009F306F" w:rsidRDefault="009F306F" w:rsidP="009F306F"><w:pPr><w:spacing w:line="360" w:lineRule="auto"/><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:b/><w:bCs/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr></w:pPr><w:r w:rsidRPr="009F306F"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:b/><w:bCs/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t>Understanding Professionalism</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="4DD75FB9" w14:textId="55D021F3" w:rsidR="009F306F" w:rsidRDefault="009F306F" w:rsidP="009F306F"><w:pPr><w:spacing w:line="360" w:lineRule="auto"/><w:ind w:firstLine="720"/><w:jc w:val="both"/><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr></w:pPr><w:r w:rsidRPr="009F306F"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t>For me, professionalism as an Information Technology Professional includes not just the abilities I can use but how I execute them. As a student of BSIT, being professional as an Information Technology Professional means not only being proficient in programming, system design and development, troublesho</w:t></w:r><w:r w:rsidR="00911007"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t>o</w:t></w:r><w:r w:rsidRPr="009F306F"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t>ting computer and know how to operate any computer system or gadget, but as well, being honest, showing respect and gratitude to other, being responsible of what they perform and not being shy to learn something new. Although, all of that skills has no importance at all since all information IT Professional deal is with people, data or resources and machinery.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="3B33AC8D" w14:textId="078D2BD6" w:rsidR="009F306F" w:rsidRPr="009F306F" w:rsidRDefault="009F306F" w:rsidP="009F306F"><w:pPr><w:spacing w:line="360" w:lineRule="auto"/><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:b/><w:bCs/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr></w:pPr><w:r w:rsidRPr="009F306F"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:b/><w:bCs/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t>Personal Qualities</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="15D70D12" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="009F306F" w:rsidRDefault="009F306F" w:rsidP="009F306F"><w:pPr><w:spacing w:line="360" w:lineRule="auto"/><w:ind w:firstLine="720"/><w:jc w:val="both"/><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr></w:pPr><w:r w:rsidRPr="009F306F"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t>Considering the traits of a professional IT practitioner. I would say my strongest trait is my responsibility. I do value my assignments in school and my organization activities especially with the thought of my groupmates relying on me when it comes to finishing my tasks. When I started my BSIT course, I have become part of the programming and system development projects in which problems and time are both important factors that you should deal with.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="470FB92A" w14:textId="671CC576" w:rsidR="009F306F" w:rsidRPr="009F306F" w:rsidRDefault="009F306F" w:rsidP="009F306F"><w:pPr><w:spacing w:line="360" w:lineRule="auto"/><w:ind w:firstLine="720"/><w:jc w:val="both"/><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr></w:pPr><w:r w:rsidRPr="009F306F"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t>I also find enjoyment when trouble-shooting issues for I like to trace the roots of each problems</w:t></w:r><w:r w:rsidR="00911007"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t>,</w:t></w:r><w:r w:rsidRPr="009F306F"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t xml:space="preserve"> that I encounter and consider using trials and errors as part of the solutions. But still I have issues in terms of my dependability and managing my time properly, I tend to spend a long time in modifying and improving the program for the purpose of perfecting it, I need to train myself on how I should control the managing part of this while I must still achieve the quality.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="56608771" w14:textId="033EEE65" w:rsidR="009F306F" w:rsidRPr="009F306F" w:rsidRDefault="009F306F" w:rsidP="009F306F"><w:pPr><w:spacing w:line="360" w:lineRule="auto"/><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:b/><w:bCs/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr></w:pPr><w:r w:rsidRPr="009F306F"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:b/><w:bCs/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t>Ethical Responsibility</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="78476A8C" w14:textId="22A79609" w:rsidR="009F306F" w:rsidRPr="009F306F" w:rsidRDefault="009F306F" w:rsidP="009F306F"><w:pPr><w:spacing w:line="360" w:lineRule="auto"/><w:ind w:firstLine="720"/><w:jc w:val="both"/><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr></w:pPr><w:r w:rsidRPr="009F306F"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t xml:space="preserve">IT Confidentiality and Privacy The information system is being used by these days that is having confidential as well as not Confidential as well, the Professional may know Passwords of anyone, some of the individuals personal information such as Name of </w:t></w:r><w:proofErr w:type="spellStart"/><w:r w:rsidRPr="009F306F"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t>there</w:t></w:r><w:proofErr w:type="spellEnd"/><w:r w:rsidRPr="009F306F"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t xml:space="preserve"> Family, friends etc., some other may know about the databases and </w:t></w:r><w:proofErr w:type="spellStart"/><w:r w:rsidRPr="009F306F"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t>there</w:t></w:r><w:proofErr w:type="spellEnd"/><w:r w:rsidRPr="009F306F"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t xml:space="preserve"> contents </w:t></w:r><w:proofErr w:type="spellStart"/><w:r w:rsidRPr="009F306F"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t>etc</w:t></w:r><w:proofErr w:type="spellEnd"/><w:r w:rsidRPr="009F306F"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t>, so if I know this information, I am duty bound that I should not show these confidential files or databases to other and should not misuse this information etc. So that people will have respect for each other’s.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="1A30356A" w14:textId="4215123F" w:rsidR="009F306F" w:rsidRPr="009F306F" w:rsidRDefault="009F306F" w:rsidP="009F306F"><w:pPr><w:spacing w:line="360" w:lineRule="auto"/><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:b/><w:bCs/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr></w:pPr><w:r w:rsidRPr="009F306F"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:b/><w:bCs/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:lastRenderedPageBreak/><w:t>Professional Conduct</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="57A68F9D" w14:textId="2CB33834" w:rsidR="009F306F" w:rsidRDefault="009F306F" w:rsidP="009F306F"><w:pPr><w:spacing w:line="360" w:lineRule="auto"/><w:ind w:firstLine="720"/><w:jc w:val="both"/><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr></w:pPr><w:r w:rsidRPr="009F306F"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t>In school, it helps me be professional in doing my group projects. I have to be punctual in the assigned jobs that each groupmate has. I need to tell my groupmates as I have difficulty on those works, take into account and give chance to groupmates’ ideas, accept their criticism of my</w:t></w:r><w:r w:rsidR="00911007"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t xml:space="preserve"> </w:t></w:r><w:r w:rsidRPr="009F306F"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t>work. It is important to admit mistakes instead of passing blame, and willing to have groups efforts together in resolving it as professional workplace expects.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="2C3C4F6D" w14:textId="1907B48F" w:rsidR="009F306F" w:rsidRPr="009F306F" w:rsidRDefault="009F306F" w:rsidP="009F306F"><w:pPr><w:spacing w:line="360" w:lineRule="auto"/><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:b/><w:bCs/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr></w:pPr><w:r w:rsidRPr="009F306F"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:b/><w:bCs/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t>Cybersecurity Responsibility</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="424007DC" w14:textId="2E4C9A71" w:rsidR="00B061F4" w:rsidRPr="00B061F4" w:rsidRDefault="00B061F4" w:rsidP="00B061F4"><w:pPr><w:spacing w:line="360" w:lineRule="auto"/><w:ind w:firstLine="720"/><w:jc w:val="both"/><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr></w:pPr><w:r w:rsidRPr="00B061F4"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t xml:space="preserve">As a IT student, if I had found out that my classmate or colleague had his/her password on sticky note and stick on his/her desktop then what will I do is respect the user privacy not taking advantage on it or tell anyone else I would in person told her/his that “I notice that </w:t></w:r><w:proofErr w:type="spellStart"/><w:r w:rsidRPr="00B061F4"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t>your</w:t></w:r><w:proofErr w:type="spellEnd"/><w:r w:rsidR="00911007"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t xml:space="preserve"> </w:t></w:r><w:r w:rsidRPr="00B061F4"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t>have write down password on your laptop, please write it on somewhere safer like in a little note book and change password regularly because it will risk your account.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="4F091865" w14:textId="1871F81F" w:rsidR="009F306F" w:rsidRPr="009F306F" w:rsidRDefault="009F306F" w:rsidP="009F306F"><w:pPr><w:spacing w:line="360" w:lineRule="auto"/><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:b/><w:bCs/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr></w:pPr><w:r w:rsidRPr="009F306F"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:b/><w:bCs/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t>Digital Professionalism</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="08C97FA0" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="00B061F4" w:rsidRPr="00B061F4" w:rsidRDefault="00B061F4" w:rsidP="00B061F4"><w:pPr><w:spacing w:line="360" w:lineRule="auto"/><w:ind w:firstLine="720"/><w:jc w:val="both"/><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr></w:pPr><w:r w:rsidRPr="00B061F4"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t>How my communication on social media, comment sections and general online interaction would impact my reputation and profile as an IT student &amp; future professional; I should be aware of what I post / share, respect others, and refrain from sharing personal or proprietary information. Ideally my interactions online would always present a more professional version of me.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="49BD575D" w14:textId="621F6890" w:rsidR="009F306F" w:rsidRPr="009F306F" w:rsidRDefault="009F306F" w:rsidP="009F306F"><w:pPr><w:spacing w:line="360" w:lineRule="auto"/><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:b/><w:bCs/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr></w:pPr><w:r w:rsidRPr="009F306F"><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:b/><w:bCs/><w:sz w:val="24"/><w:szCs w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t>Continuous Learning</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="67FDA651" w14:textId="1D6C1CB8" w:rsidR="00B061F4" w:rsidRDefault="00B061F4" w:rsidP="00B061F4"><w:pPr><w:spacing w:line="360" w:lin